{"title": "List of equipment of the Ecuadorian Armed Forces", "revid": 1381415211, "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_equipment_of_the_Ecuadorian_Armed_Forces", "tables": [{"sec": "Army / Armoured fighting vehicles", "hdr": ["model", "image", "origin", "quantity", "details"], "rows": [[], [], ["Light tanks", "Light tanks", "Light tanks", "Light tanks", "Light tanks"], ["AMX-13", "", "France", "~108", "In 1988, Ecuador upgraded its fleet of 108 AMX-13 light tanks armed with 105 mm guns. SOPELEM supplied the basic day version of its SOPTAC 18 fire-control system with laser rangefinder and its control unit. Fives-Cail Babcock provided kits to modify the 105 mm gun and its ammunition system to allow APFSDS rounds to be fired. Work on upgrading the AMX-13s started in Ecuador late in 1988 and was completed in 1990."], ["Reconnaissance vehicle", "Reconnaissance vehicle", "Reconnaissance vehicle", "Reconnaissance vehicle", "Reconnaissance vehicle"], ["EE-3 Jararaca", "", "Brazil", "~10", ""], ["EE-9 Cascavel", "", "Brazil", "~32", ""], ["Armoured personnel carriers", "Armoured personnel carriers", "Armoured personnel carriers", "Armoured personnel carriers", "Armoured personnel carriers"], ["AMX-VCI", "", "France", "~82", ""], ["M113", "", "United States", "~20", ""], ["EE-11 Urutu", "", "Brazil", "~17", ""], ["UR-416", "", "West Germany", "~32", ""], ["Cobra II", "", "Turkey", "~20", ""]]}, {"sec": "Army / Artillery", "hdr": ["model", "image", "origin", "caliber", "quantity", "details"], "rows": [["Mortar", "Mortar", "Mortar", "Mortar", "Mortar", "Mortar"], ["M29", "", "United States", "81mm", "~357", ""], ["Towed", "Towed", "Towed", "Towed", "Towed", "Towed"], ["Model 56 pack", "", "Italy", "105mm", "~24", ""], ["M101", "", "United States", "105mm", "~36", ""], ["M2A2", "", "United States", "105mm", "~24", ""], ["M114", "", "United States", "155mm", "~12", ""], ["M198", "", "United States", "155mm", "~10", ""], ["Self-propelled", "Self-propelled", "Self-propell